|##
import "speed_run.malloy"

##|(markdown) intro
## 1. Each replay

A query replay re-runs the query behind every passing answer and times it, with
no agent and no judge. `total_ms` is the sum of each query's median. Read the
version beside it: a replay of an unbuilt persist times the live query.
|##

##|(markdown) comparing
## 2. Against the baseline

The first replay is the baseline. Rows come first: any query in `blocked_queries`
changed its answer, and a speed edit with one there is not accepted. Speed counts
only over queries whose rows held, and only past the replay's band. Before
trusting a small change, compare two replays of the same version: that gap is
the noise on this machine.
|##

##|(markdown) where_time_goes
## 3. Where the time goes

Time per source tells you which one a `#@ persist` or `#@ preaggregate` would
pay off on. The slowest queries are the ones a diagnose finding names.
|##
